{
  "intro": "Possessive adjectives show who owns something. In Spanish, mi, tu, su, and nuestro go before the noun they describe.",
  "overview": {
    "body": "Possessive adjectives agree with the thing possessed. Their form depends on the noun that follows, not on the owner's gender.",
    "use_note": "Agreement with the noun"
  },
  "examples": [
    {
      "spanish": "Mi libro está aquí.",
      "english": "My book is here."
    },
    {
      "spanish": "Mis libros están aquí.",
      "english": "My books are here."
    }
  ],
  "forms": [
    {
      "label": "mi / mis",
      "meaning": "my"
    },
    {
      "label": "tu / tus",
      "meaning": "your (informal singular)"
    },
    {
      "label": "su / sus",
      "meaning": "his, her, your formal, their, your plural"
    },
    {
      "label": "nuestro / nuestra / nuestros / nuestras",
      "meaning": "our"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Mi, tu, and su change between singular and plural according to the noun: mi libro / mis libros; tu amigo / tus amigos; su pregunta / sus preguntas.",
    "Nuestro changes for masculine, feminine, singular, and plural nouns: nuestro libro, nuestra casa, nuestros libros, nuestras casas.",
    "Tu (without an accent) is possessive; tú (with an accent) is the subject pronoun.",
    "Su / sus can refer to different owners. Context helps identify whose noun it is."
  ],
  "uses": [
    {
      "heading": "Possessive adjectives before the noun",
      "body": "Place mi, tu, su, and nuestro before the noun. The singular and plural forms describe how many things are possessed.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "spanish": "Tu teléfono está en la mesa.",
          "english": "Your phone is on the table."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Sus amigos viven en Chile.",
          "english": "His, her, your formal, or their friends live in Chile."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Our: gender and number",
      "body": "Nuestro agrees with the noun in both gender and number.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "spanish": "Nuestra clase empieza ahora.",
          "english": "Our class starts now."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Nuestros profesores trabajan aquí.",
          "english": "Our teachers work here."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
